WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.617
Now we focus on corrective rag.

00:00:02.617 --> 00:00:08.227
The loop has three broad actions: retrieve, judge, and correct.

00:00:08.227 --> 00:00:11.442
First, retrieve candidate evidence.

00:00:11.442 --> 00:00:18.107
Second, judge whether that evidence is relevant, sufficient, authoritative, and current enough.

00:00:18.107 --> 00:00:21.357
Third, correct only if necessary.

00:00:21.357 --> 00:00:28.672
Correction may mean rewriting the query, selecting another source, applying a filter, asking the user,

00:00:28.672 --> 00:00:30.227
or stopping safely.

00:00:30.711 --> 00:00:35.153
Retrieval quality is not one simple yes or no property.

00:00:35.153 --> 00:00:38.443
A source can be relevant but incomplete.

00:00:38.443 --> 00:00:41.118
It can be complete but outdated.

00:00:41.118 --> 00:00:44.545
It can be current but not authoritative for the decision.

00:00:44.995 --> 00:00:52.597
Corrective rag becomes useful when we can diagnose the specific retrieval problem and choose an appropriate correction

00:00:52.597 --> 00:00:54.807
rather than blindly retrying.
